{
  "_note": [
    "First PUBLIC availability of a technology, for rule D7 — a project cannot have",
    "been built with something that did not exist yet.",
    "",
    "Every date here is deliberately biased EARLY. Where a technology has both an",
    "internal-use date and a 1.0, the earlier one is recorded, because the two ways",
    "of being wrong are not symmetric: a date that is too early makes the rule miss a",
    "real anachronism, and a date that is too late makes it accuse an honest",
    "candidate. Only the first kind of error is acceptable.",
    "",
    "The rule adds a second layer of the same caution: it fires only when the release",
    "is after the project's ENTIRE max span, so a year-precision date never fires on a",
    "technology released during that year.",
    "",
    "Keys are matched after normalisation — lowercased, punctuation stripped — so",
    "'Next.js' and 'nextjs' both resolve here. An unlisted technology is unknown, not",
    "anachronistic, and the rule says nothing about it."
  ],
